## Step C1: Simplest Architecture

```
User Query → AI Application → Language Model Service → Response
```

**Main user interaction:** A student names or selects scholarships to compare and reads a table of their eligibility criteria and deadlines.

**AI capability needed:** A language model service that reads scholarship information and produces the structured criteria (citizenship, age limit, minimum results, deadline, required documents).

**Can this simple architecture satisfy the Part A and Part B requirements?**

| Requirement / Criterion | Supported by simple architecture? | Why |
|---|---|---|
| FR4 / NFR6: Clear, comparable output | Yes | The model can format criteria as a plain table. |
| NFR1: Latency | Yes | One model call per request. |
| FR5: Normalised JSON schema | Partly | A prompt can ask for a format, but the output is not validated and can be malformed or inconsistent. |
| FR2 / NFR2: Values consistent with the selected documents | No | The model has no access to the actual documents and answers from general or outdated knowledge. |
| FR3 / RAI2: Verifiable source references | No | There is no document to cite, and the model may invent a source or a deadline. |
| FR6 / RAI3: Say "not stated" when the document does not contain a field | No | Nothing tells the model whether the document contains the answer, so it tends to fill gaps with plausible values. |
| FR7 / RAI4: Refuse out-of-scope requests | Partly | An instruction can ask the model to refuse, but this is not reliable or testable on its own. |
| FR1 / NFR5 / RAI6: Add documents and record versions | No | There is no document handling or document register. |
| RAI1: Groundedness | No | Values cannot be tied to retrieved evidence. |
| NFR2 to NFR4 / RAI1 to RAI3: Evaluation evidence | No | There is nowhere to capture documents, passages, outputs, latency and cost. |

**Conclusion:** The simple flow supports clear formatting and low latency, but not grounding, source tracing, abstention, reliable scope control, document management, output validation, or evaluation. Components are added in C2 to cover these gaps.

