## Step C2: Architecture Needs from Requirements

| Requirement ID | What does the requirement need? | Architecture Response |
|---|---|---|
| FR1 / NFR5 | Scholarship PDFs and web pages must be added and become searchable without rebuilding unrelated parts. | **Document Processing** component that downloads, converts and cleans documents, separate from answering. |
| FR1 / RAI6 | Each document's title, sponsor, URL, intake year and download date must be recorded. | Document metadata held alongside the indexed content in the **Knowledge Source**. |
| FR2 / NFR2 / NFR3 | Extracted values must come from the selected documents, and the right passages must be found for each field. | **Knowledge Source** plus **Knowledge Retrieval** that returns the relevant passages for each field. |
| FR3 / RAI2 | Each value must include a reference and the supporting passage. | Passage and document metadata carried through to the response, so every cell can be traced to its source. |
| FR5 / RAI1 | Values must fit the fixed JSON schema and be supported by the passages. | **Output Validation** after extraction: a schema check plus a faithfulness check that each value appears in its source passage. |
| FR6 / RAI3 | The system must say "not stated" when the document does not contain a field. | **Evidence Sufficiency Check** between retrieval and extraction, with a "not stated" path. |
| FR7 / RAI4 | Out-of-scope requests must be refused and redirected. | **Scope / Safety Control** placed before retrieval and extraction. |
| FR2 / FR4 / NFR6 | The table must stay consistent with the sources and remain readable. | **Language Model Service** that extracts only from the retrieved passages provided to it, with the result shown as a comparison table. |
| RAI5 | Students must be told to verify against the original document. | Response format in the **Application Interface** includes a verification notice, source link and date checked. |
| NFR1 / NFR4 | Latency and cost must stay within thresholds. | **Evaluation Point** that records latency and usage; a small number of components on the main path. |
| NFR2 | Accuracy must be measured against a baseline. | **Evaluation Point** holds the ground-truth labels and the regex baseline results for field-level precision, recall and F1. |
| RAI7 | Personal identifiers must not be stored beyond the session. | Evaluation Point limited to non-personal data; no persistent user profile. |

