### Component Summary

| Component | Function | Justified by |
|---|---|---|
| Student | Selects scholarships to compare and reads the comparison table. | Target users |
| Application Interface | Accepts the student's selection or request; displays the table, source references and the verification notice. | FR4, RAI5 |
| Scope / Safety Control | Checks whether a request is in scope; refuses and redirects if not (for example "am I eligible?" or "which one should I pick?"). | FR7, RAI4 |
| Knowledge Retrieval | Finds passages in the selected documents that are relevant to each field. | FR2, NFR3 |
| Knowledge Source | Holds the indexed scholarship text and document metadata (sponsor, URL, intake year, download date). | FR1, FR3, RAI6 |
| Evidence Sufficiency Check | Decides whether the retrieved passages are enough to extract a field; returns "not stated" if not. | FR6, RAI3 |
| Language Model Service | Extracts field values from the retrieved passages and formats them for the table. | FR2, FR4, RAI1 |
| Output Validation | Checks the output against the JSON schema and checks that each value appears in its source passage. | FR5, RAI1 |
| Response / Output | Comparison table with source references and verification notice, or a refusal or "not stated" message. | FR3, FR6, FR7, RAI2, RAI5 |
| Document Sources | Approved public scholarship PDFs and web pages. | FR1, RAI6 |
| Document Processing | Prepares new documents so they can be searched (offline). | FR1, NFR5 |
| Evaluation Point | Records documents, retrieved passages, outputs, latency and cost for evaluation. | NFR1 to NFR4, RAI1 to RAI3, RAI7 |

*Components are labelled by function. Specific models, retrieval methods, databases and frameworks will be selected in later topics.*

