## Step C4: Architecture Decision Records (ADR)

| Decision | Requirement / Constraint | Alternatives Considered | Selected Option | Trade-off Accepted |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **ADR1:** Include knowledge access from the selected documents | FR2, FR3, NFR2, RAI1: values must be grounded in the selected documents and traceable to sources. | (a) Language model only; (b) pass the whole document to the model on every request; (c) retrieve relevant passages first. | Retrieve relevant passages from a Knowledge Source before extraction. | More system complexity, and extraction quality now depends on retrieval quality (a criterion split across sections may be missed). In return, values are better grounded and traceable to a specific passage. Passing whole documents is possible for short files but gives coarse source tracing and does not scale to long handbooks. |
| **ADR2:** Include an explicit evidence sufficiency check | FR6, RAI3, RAI1: the system must not fill in missing fields with guessed values. | (a) Prompt instruction only; (b) explicit check before extraction. | Explicit Evidence Sufficiency Check with a "not stated" path. | Some fields that are actually in the document will be wrongly shown as "not stated" (false abstentions), and there is a little extra processing. In return, fewer invented deadlines or criteria. |
| **ADR3:** Include an explicit scope control | FR7, RAI4: eligibility decisions, application advice and out-of-collection requests must be refused. | (a) Instruction to the model only; (b) explicit scope-control component. | Explicit Scope / Safety Control before retrieval. | Possible false refusals of borderline comparison requests, and added latency (NFR1). In return, a testable, repeatable control. |
| **ADR4:** Keep document processing separate from answering | FR1, NFR5, RAI6: new documents must be added without rebuilding the application, with versions recorded. | (a) Process documents at request time; (b) separate offline processing with a document register. | Separate Document Processing step feeding the Knowledge Source. | Documents must be prepared before use, and PDF parsing may handle tables or multi-column layouts poorly. In return, faster responses and easier maintenance. |
| **ADR5:** Include an Evaluation Point from V1 | NFR1 to NFR4, RAI1 to RAI3, RAI7: evidence is needed to show thresholds are met. | (a) Add evaluation later; (b) capture evaluation data from the start. | Evaluation Point that records non-personal interaction data. | Extra logging effort now, and care is needed to avoid storing personal data. In return, evaluation evidence is available from the first prototype. |
| **ADR6:** Include an output validation step | FR5, RAI1: values must fit the fixed schema and be supported by the source passage. | (a) Trust the model's output; (b) prompt for JSON only; (c) explicit schema and faithfulness check. | Explicit Output Validation after the Language Model Service. | Some valid outputs may be rejected and need re-extraction, which adds processing and cost. In return, malformed or unsupported values are caught before they reach the student. |

